 between nature, or the environment, and culture, or society, and whether these should be viewed as separate domains at all. How one answers this question has important implications for how we go about thinking and acting in such diverse social arenas as environmental politics, development, and indigenous-state relations. This course serves as an introduction to the various ways anthropologists and other scholars have conceptualized the relationship between humans and the environment and considers the material and political consequences that flow from these conceptualizations.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": null, "catalogEnrollmentPriority": "", "catalogLang": null, "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": null, "catalogAttribute": null, "catalogWhenOffered": null, "catalogComments": null, "catalogPrereqCoreq": null, "catalogPrereq": "", "catalogCoreq": "", "catalogFee": null, "catalogSatisfiesReq": null, "catalogPermission": null, "catalogCourseSubfield": null, "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AG", "catalogName": null, "catalogNextOffered": null, "lastTermsOffered": "2025FA, 2024FA, 2023FA, 2021FA", "catalogCredits": null, "catalogGradeOption": null, "catalogLocation": null, "catalogCrosslisted": null, "catalogCrosslistings": null, "catalogComeets": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2909, "crseId": 359320, "crseOfferNbr": 4, "subject": "AIIS", "catalogNbr": "3248", "titleShort": "Northeast Native Archaeology", "titleLong": "Finger Lakes and Beyond: Archaeology of the Native Northeast", "crseAttrs": [{"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "HA-AG", "descr": "AG-Historical Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Historical Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue": "SBA-AG", "descr": "AG-Social & Behvl Analysis", "descrformal": "AG-Social and Behavioral Analysis", "attrDescr": "Distribution Requirements", "attrDescrShort": "DistReq"}, {"crseAttr": "0012", "crseAttrValue"